response.answer:
Simply put, the admissions team must confirm:

- whether your education, English qualification, questionnaire, references, and international credential evaluation are acceptable;
- whether alternate-entry applicants have enough computing knowledge or need bridging courses;
- how your complete application ranks against others.

Meeting the minimum requirements does **not** guarantee admission.

[Applied Computing MSc details](https://www.bcit.ca/programs/applied-computing-master-of-science-full-time-m600msc/)

